this is a Michigan made 268 thousand  dollar supercar called the force one and  it's supposed to be the American answer  to everything that acid Martin or  McLaren can produce the Force One is the  latest brainchild from former General  Motors vice-chairman Bob Lutz and  celebrity car designer Henrik Fisker  this car you want to keep it exclusive  because we can cater to people who says  you know I already have a Range Rover I  already have a rolls-royce already got a  BMW 7-series but I want something really  unique something and nobody else have  something to have fun with and obvious  you have the money and then you buy this  type of stuff now this car is a little  controversial because Aston Martin has  claimed that Fisker is using some of the  main design elements that make aston  stevie 10 unique Fisker actually used to  work for aston martin but from the first  moment you see the force 1 you'll  realize there is absolutely no way  anyone would mistake it for an aston  martin the force 1 is characterized by  its enormous front end wheels push  incredibly close to the tip of the nose  a super long hood with massive air vents  a short windshield and a tight rounded  roof that swoops down into the rear the  spoiler on the rear end sets high and  holds the mechanics for the cars Wi-Fi  and for its rear brake lights it's all  meant to follow the flow of air as it  moves over this v10 machine the rear  window ends in a tiny wisp which is  unique to the Force One and it's  certainly the prettiest part of the car  the rest of it looks a little too much  like half a Corvette with maybe parts of  a Viper thrown in as well Fisker says  though that he already has people lining  up to buy one and he claims that he only  needs to build a handful of them anyway  to break even  he says he'll make about a hundred or so  in the first round it's an expensive  hobby making new cars like this but  Fisker doesn't seem to be in it for the  money for him it's about making very  special cars
 

